<<~ ahu #/law>>

! The law of the ledger

One tree, several hearths. A hearth names a session by the `Claude-Session:` trailer its commits carry — never a person, never a model. The ledger answers three questions any hand must read before touching shared ground: ''who holds what'' (files and regions a hearth is mid-edit in), ''what each owes'' (the loud reds and rulings another hearth waits on), and ''what crossed'' (a seam one hearth ceded to another, with the commit that carried it). `git status` reads the dirt; this carrier reads the ''intent'' behind it.

A row moves when a hearth seals a region, cedes a seam, or takes one. A crossing without a row here reads as the failure this ledger exists to end.

<<~/ahu>>

